From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Domurad <domuradical@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 18:34:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ci3): the dashboard serves the ci3 server API

Adds ci3_api.py, registered by rk.py: the API in aztec-packages' ci3/CI3_SERVER_API.md on the
dashboard's redis and S3, with the key shapes the dashboard already renders. Every route takes the
dashboard's basic auth, which the ci3 client sends from ~/.ci3/config.json once it is pointed here.

The API refuses to serve without a password; bodies and gzip expansion are bounded; log and kv
writes cannot cross into the run and list families; runs are validated, stored compact and
replaced atomically; a redis outage does not lose a final log; only genuine absence is a 404.
Alongside: constant-time password comparison, quoted /grind arguments, redis and S3 client
timeouts. ci3_api_test.py covers it against a real redis and an in-memory S3.

